  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is glibenclamide, an arylsulfonylurea sharing the N-phenethyl arylsulfonylurea-cyclohexylurea core with glimepiride; the closest context L1 records report essentially complete absolute oral bioavailability in humans, reinforced by L2 records.",
      "card_ids": ["C03", "C16", "C19", "C24", "C31", "C39"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for glimepiride fixed-dose combinations show measurable Cmax values after oral dosing, consistent with substantial absorption, though they lack an IV comparator.",
      "card_ids": ["C46", "C47"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 records show glimepiride low aqueous solubility but rapid dissolution from enabling formulations (C53, C55, C61, C62); glipizide human FA >95% despite low solubility (C54, C58, C60), supporting the sulfonylurea class pattern that low solubility does not imply low F.",
      "card_ids": ["C53", "C54", "C55", "C58", "C60", "C61", "C62"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 records are mechanistic gut-wall efflux/transport experiments for gliquidone, glipizide, talinolol, and sulpiride; none is a direct F measurement for the query. Gliquidone is a P-gp/BCRP substrate (C70, C73), and talinolol/sulpiride P-gp effects (C66, C68, C74, C75) show efflux can limit exposure in those molecules, but this does not affirmatively establish F<20 for glibenclamide.",
      "card_ids": ["C66", "C68", "C70", "C73", "C74", "C75"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No transferable direct low F outcome for the query or its closest analog is present; P-gp substrate status alone is not threshold-relevant negative evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C70", "C73"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C64", "C65", "C66", "C67", "C68", "C69", "C70", "C71", "C72", "C73", "C74", "C75"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the exact query molecule glibenclamide is supplied; the high prediction relies on transfer from the closely related glimepiride context.",
    "L5 efflux records are for gliquidone, talinolol, sulpiride, and glipizide, not the query; no query-specific P-gp/BCRP or intestinal metabolism data are provided.",
    "No query-specific dose, formulation, prandial state, or species data are supplied.",
    "L3 glimepiride exposure records lack an IV comparator and do not quantify F.",
    "L4 solubility and dissolution records are formulation-specific and for other sulfonylureas, not the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high. Direct human absolute F for the closest context glimepiride is essentially complete (C03, C16, C19, C24; C31, C39), L3 exposure records are consistent (C46, C47), and L4 confirms the class pattern of high permeability/absorption despite low solubility (C54). L5 adds only mechanistic P-gp/BCRP efflux data for other molecules (e.g., gliquidone C70, C73) and does not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F<20 in the query; P-gp substrate status alone is not a low-F result. Confidence high; revision keep."
}

